Fare rules: flight 1 of 2, traveler 1 of 2

1. Changes before departure
1.1 A change made before the first flight on this ticket carries no
change fee.
1.2 The new flight must be in the same cabin or a higher one, and any
difference in fare is collected when the change is made.
1.3 When the new fare is lower, the difference is kept as travel credit
in the name of the traveler on the ticket.
1.4 A change must be made no later than the scheduled departure time of
the flight that is being changed.
1.5 A change to one traveler on the record does not change the tickets
of any other traveler on it.
1.6 Where a change moves travel into a period with higher fares, the
higher fare applies.

2. Changes after departure
2.1 Once the first flight has been flown, the flights that remain may be
moved only to another date or time on the same route.
2.2 The starting point of the next flight may not be changed once travel
has begun.
2.3 A change after departure is priced at the fare on offer on the day
the change is made.
2.4 A change made at the airport on the day of travel depends on seats
being free on the new flight.

3. Cancellation and refunds
3.1 This ticket is non-refundable except where the law requires a
refund.
3.2 A ticket canceled within 24 hours of purchase, and at least seven
days before departure, is refunded in full to the card that paid for it.
3.3 After that period the value of a canceled ticket is kept as travel
credit, in full or less a fee, as rule 39 sets out.
3.4 Taxes collected for flights that are not flown may be refunded on
request.
3.5 A request for a refund must be made within one year of the day the
ticket was issued.

4. Travel credit
4.1 Travel credit may be used toward a new ticket for the same traveler
and has no cash value.
4.2 Credit must be used to book new travel before it expires; the travel
itself may take place later.
4.3 When a new ticket costs less than the credit, what is left stays as
credit with the same expiry.
4.4 Credit may not be passed to another person, sold or exchanged.

5. Missed flights
5.1 If a traveler does not take a flight and does not cancel it before
departure, every later flight on the same ticket is canceled.
5.2 A ticket marked as not flown keeps no value, apart from taxes that
may be refunded on request.
5.3 A traveler who reaches the gate after boarding has closed is treated
as not having flown.
5.4 A traveler who misses a flight because an earlier flight on the same
ticket ran late is moved to the next flight with a free seat at no
charge.

6. Names on tickets
6.1 The name on the ticket must match the photo ID the traveler shows at
the airport.
6.2 A small correction, such as one wrong letter, may be made without a
new ticket.
6.3 A ticket may not be transferred to another person.
6.4 A legal change of name needs proof and is handled by the
reservations desk.

7. Schedule changes by the airline
7.1 The airline may change flight times, flight numbers or aircraft
after a ticket is issued.
7.2 When a schedule change moves a departure by more than ninety
minutes, the traveler may choose another flight at no charge or ask for
a refund.
7.3 Notice of a schedule change is sent to the email address on the
record.

8. Delays and cancellations by the airline
8.1 If the airline cancels a flight, the traveler is rebooked on the
next flight with a free seat in the same cabin.
8.2 A traveler who chooses not to travel after a cancellation by the
airline is owed a refund of the unused part of the ticket.
8.3 Meals and a hotel room may be offered for long delays that are
within the airline's control.
8.4 Delays caused by weather or by air traffic control are outside the
airline's control.

9. Checked bags
9.1 Checked bags are not included in this fare unless the receipt says
otherwise.
9.2 Each checked bag may weigh up to 57 pounds and measure up to 71
inches in length, width and height added together.
9.3 Bags over the weight or size limit carry an extra charge and may be
refused.
9.4 Fees for checked bags are charged for each direction of travel.
9.5 Bags must be checked at least 53 minutes before the scheduled
departure.

10. Carry-on items
10.1 Each traveler may bring one carry-on bag and one personal item on
board.
10.2 A carry-on bag must fit in the overhead bin, and a personal item
under the seat in front.
10.3 An item that does not fit may be checked at the gate, and a fee may
apply.

11. Seats
11.1 Seat assignments are not guaranteed and may change for operational
reasons.
11.2 A seat bought for an extra charge is refunded if the airline moves
the traveler to a seat of lower value.
11.3 Seats in exit rows are offered only to travelers who are willing
and able to help in an emergency.

12. Children and infants
12.1 A child under two years old may travel on an adult's lap on flights
within the country.
12.2 An infant on a lap must travel with an adult who is at least 18
years old.
12.3 A child who turns two during the trip needs a seat of their own for
every flight after the birthday.
12.4 Children traveling without an adult must be booked through the
reservations desk, and an extra charge applies.

13. Pets
13.1 Small cats and dogs may travel in the cabin in a carrier that fits
under the seat.
13.2 A pet in the cabin counts as the traveler's carry-on bag.
13.3 The number of pets on each flight is limited, so a pet must be
added to the booking in advance.

14. Sports and special items
14.1 Golf clubs, skis and bicycles may be checked as one bag when packed
in a hard case.
14.2 Musical instruments may travel in the cabin when they fit in the
overhead bin.
14.3 Items too large for the cabin may be checked for an extra charge.

15. Combining fares
15.1 This fare may be combined with other one-way fares in the same
cabin.
15.2 When two fares are combined, the stricter of the two sets of rules
applies to the whole ticket.
15.3 A round trip priced as one fare must be flown in order.

16. Length of stay
16.1 No minimum stay is required.
16.2 The return flight must be flown within one year of the outbound
flight.
16.3 A stop of more than four hours between connecting flights is not
allowed on this fare.

17. Upgrades
17.1 Upgrades depend on availability and are confirmed only when shown
on the ticket.
17.2 A paid upgrade applies to the flights shown and is not refundable
once the first upgraded flight has been flown.
17.3 Upgrades paid for with miles or points are not available on this
fare.

18. Payment
18.1 The price of the ticket is charged in full at the time of booking.
18.2 The card used to pay may need to be shown at check-in.
18.3 A payment in another currency is converted by the card issuer,
which may add a fee.

19. Check-in and boarding
19.1 Check-in closes 47 minutes before departure on flights within the
country.
19.2 Boarding begins about 38 minutes before departure, and the aircraft
door closes 13 minutes before departure.
19.3 A traveler who has not checked in by the cut-off time may lose the
seat.

20. Conduct
20.1 The airline may refuse to carry a traveler whose conduct puts the
safety of the flight at risk.
20.2 A traveler refused for conduct is not owed a refund.

21. Help at the airport
21.1 Wheelchair help is free of charge and should be asked for at least
48 hours before departure.
21.2 Trained service animals travel free of charge in the cabin.

22. Taxes and fees
22.1 Government taxes and fees are set by the authorities and may change
